  "demographic_questions": {
    "header": "Voluntary Self ID Questionnaire (Canada)",
    "description": "<p>At Instacart, we like to think of ourselves as a potluck&mdash;where everyone brings something new, different, and flavorful to the table. We believe our team&rsquo;s wide range of perspectives, experiences and backgrounds enable us to build a better product for our customers. Instacart is for everyone, and we&rsquo;re committed to fostering diverse and inclusive teams that reflect the communities we serve.</p>\n<p>Individuals seeking employment at Instacart are considered without regards to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, or any other protected characteristic.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Please note:</span> If you apply for more than one job, you will be asked to fill out the questionnaire for each application.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>How is this information used?</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In order to track our effectiveness in recruiting a wide range of talent and to ensure that we comply with reporting requirements, we invite all applicants to voluntarily provide demographic information in a confidential survey. Providing this information is entirely optional. It is only used to ensure our hiring efforts remain free of bias and for diversity monitoring purposes. Data collected is not factored into the hiring decision or thereafter and will not affect your opportunity for employment at Instacart.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Who has access to this data?</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To ensure our hiring efforts are equitable, data is stored confidentially in our ATS (Applicant Tracking System) where only an Administrator can view demographic reporting. It is not accessible to hiring teams. Data is stored securely in a cloud-based data-warehouse to create anonymized dashboards that select HR leaders can reference.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Self-identification categories&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Gender Identity:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> How a person identifies their gender, regardless of their gender assigned at birth.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><strong>2SLGBTQIA+</strong>: An umbrella term for a range of sexual orientations and gender identities/expressions. Stands for \"Two-Spirit, Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender, Queer, Intersex, and Asexual. The plus sign is meant to encompass all other identities that belong to this community.\"</li>\n<li><strong>Race/Ethnicity:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> A person&rsquo;s racial, ethnic or origin identity.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><strong>Disability Status:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> A person&rsquo;s physical or mental impairment which may limit one or more of their major life activities. </span><a href=\"https://www.canada.ca/en/government/publicservice/wellness-inclusion-diversity-public-service/diversity-inclusion-public-service/self-identification/employee-self-identification-form.html\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Learn more here.&nbsp;</span></a></li>\n<li><strong>Veteran Status:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> A person who has spent time serving in any branch of the military (retired or active).</span></li>\n</ul>",
